IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`

-- Welfare Reform Act 2012 (United Kingdom), 2012 c. 5, Part 5, ss 121 to 126: cautions, tax credit fraud (investigation,
-- information-sharing, prosecution and penalties), and the transfer of tax credit functions. Layer 1, part wra4.
-- Host Acts named in labels: SSFA (Social Security Fraud Act 2001), SSAA (Social Security Administration Act 1992), TCA (Tax
-- Credits Act 2002). Other Acts named in the text: CJA2003 (Criminal Justice Act 2003).
-- Result convention: JUST FALSE / FALSE = the text says no; NOTHING = not covered (see wra4-ss96-97.l4).

§ `s 121 -- cautions`

-- 121(1)(c): SSFA 6B(1)(c) (cautions) is repealed. 121(2) does the same to TCA 36A(1)(c); that function is
-- `s 121(2) TCA 36A(1)(c) a caution is a ground for subsection (4)` in wra4-s120-taxcredits.l4. The printed text of
-- ss 118 and 120 still speaks of cautions (6B(11A)(c) and 36A(7)(c)): see the findings.
-- src:2161 | (c) subsection (1)(c) (cautions) is repealed;
@ref s 121(1)(c) SSFA 6B(1)(c) (src:2161-2161)
GIVEN `the person is cautioned in respect of one or more benefit offences` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Are you cautioned in respect of one or more benefit offences?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(1)(c) SSFA 6B(1)(c) a caution is a ground for the loss of benefit` MEANS
    IF `the person is cautioned in respect of one or more benefit offences`
    THEN JUST FALSE                                       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (1)(c) (cautions) is repealed"
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the repeal removes the caution ground; it says nothing about the other grounds

§ `s 122 -- tax credit fraud: investigation`

-- SSAA 109A(9): sections 109A to 109C apply as if (a) the Tax Credits Act 2002 were relevant social security legislation
-- and (b) accordingly child tax credit and working tax credit were relevant social security benefits for "benefit offence".
-- src:2168 | (a) the Tax Credits Act 2002 were relevant social security legislation, and
@ref s 122 SSAA 109A(9)(a) (src:2168-2168)
GIVEN `the legislation is the Tax Credits Act 2002` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the legislation in question the Tax Credits Act 2002?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122 SSAA 109A(9)(a) the legislation is treated as relevant social security legislation` MEANS
    IF `the legislation is the Tax Credits Act 2002`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the subsection treats this Act as relevant social security legislation; it says nothing of any other

-- src:2169 | (b) accordingly, child tax credit and working tax credit were relevant social security benefits for the purposes of the definition of “benefit offence“.
@ref s 122 SSAA 109A(9)(b) (src:2169-2169)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit  @desc Which benefit is in question?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 122 SSAA 109A(9)(b) the benefit is treated as a relevant social security benefit for the definition of benefit offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the benefit`
    WHEN `child tax credit` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `working tax credit` THEN JUST TRUE
    OTHERWISE NOTHING                                     -- NOTHING-kind (limited by own wording): the paragraph adds child tax credit and working tax credit to the benefits in question; it says nothing of any other

§ `s 123 -- information-sharing for the prevention of tax credit fraud`

-- SSAA 122B(3)(d) (inserted): "it is supplied under section 127 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012". The words of 122B(3) that
-- lead into its paragraphs are not printed, so the paragraph is answered only when it is met.
-- src:2176 | (c) after paragraph (c) there is inserted
-- src:2177 | or
-- src:2178 | (d) it is supplied under section 127 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012.
@ref s 123(3)(c) SSAA 122B(3)(d) (src:2176-2178)
GIVEN `the information is supplied under section 127 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the information supplied under section 127 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012 (information-sharing between the Secretary of State and HMRC)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 123(3)(c) SSAA 122B(3)(d) paragraph (d) is met` MEANS
    IF `the information is supplied under section 127 of the Welfare Reform Act 2012`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING                                          -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the opening words of SSAA 122B(3) that say what its paragraphs do are not among the sources

§ `s 124 -- tax credit fraud: prosecution and penalties (TCA 35)`

DECLARE `s 124 TCA 35 mode of trial` IS ONE OF
    `s 124 TCA 35(2) triable summarily only`
    `s 124 TCA 35(5) triable either on indictment or summarily`

-- TCA 35(2): payments of a tax credit not exceeding 20,000 pounds: triable summarily only. 35(5): in any other case,
-- triable either on indictment or summarily.
-- src:2181 | (2) Where a person is alleged to have committed an offence under this section in relation to payments of a tax credit not exceeding £20,000, the offence is triable summarily only.
-- src:2186 | (5) Where a person is alleged to have committed an offence under this section in any other case, the offence is triable either on indictment or summarily.
@ref s 124 TCA 35(2), (5) (src:2181-2186)
GIVEN `the payments of tax credit in relation to which the offence is alleged, in pounds` IS A NUMBER  @desc How much tax credit was paid in relation to which the offence is alleged, in pounds?
GIVETH A `s 124 TCA 35 mode of trial`
`s 124 TCA 35(2) the mode of trial` MEANS
    IF `the payments of tax credit in relation to which the offence is alleged, in pounds` AT MOST 20000
    THEN `s 124 TCA 35(2) triable summarily only`
    ELSE `s 124 TCA 35(5) triable either on indictment or summarily`

DECLARE `s 124 TCA 35 term of imprisonment` IS ONE OF
    `s 124 TCA 35(4)(a) a term of 51 weeks`
    `s 124 TCA 35 a term of 6 months`
    `s 124 TCA 35(7)(a) a term of 12 months`
    `s 124 TCA 35(6)(b) a term of 7 years`

DECLARE `s 124 TCA 35 limit of a fine` IS ONE OF
    `s 124 TCA 35(3) level 5 on the standard scale`
    `s 124 TCA 35(6)(a) the statutory maximum`
    `s 124 TCA 35(6)(b) a fine without a stated limit`

-- A punishment is "imprisonment for a term not exceeding" the term, or a fine not exceeding the limit, or both.
DECLARE `s 124 TCA 35 punishment` HAS
    `the term of imprisonment not exceeded` IS A `s 124 TCA 35 term of imprisonment`
    `the fine not exceeded`                 IS A `s 124 TCA 35 limit of a fine`

-- 35(4): the applicable term for 35(3): (a) conviction in England and Wales 51 weeks; (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland 6 months.
-- src:2183 | (4) In subsection (3) the applicable term is—
-- src:2184 | (a) for conviction in England and Wales, 51 weeks;
-- src:2185 | (b) for conviction in Scotland or Northern Ireland, 6 months.
@ref s 124 TCA 35(4) (src:2183-2185)
GIVEN `the place of conviction` IS A Place  @desc Where would you be convicted?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 124 TCA 35 term of imprisonment`
`s 124 TCA 35(4) the applicable term` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place of conviction`
    WHEN `Greater London` THEN JUST `s 124 TCA 35(4)(a) a term of 51 weeks`
    WHEN `England outside Greater London` THEN JUST `s 124 TCA 35(4)(a) a term of 51 weeks`
    WHEN Wales THEN JUST `s 124 TCA 35(4)(a) a term of 51 weeks`
    WHEN Scotland THEN JUST `s 124 TCA 35 a term of 6 months`
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN JUST `s 124 TCA 35 a term of 6 months`
    WHEN `outside the United Kingdom` THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (4) gives a term only for conviction in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland

-- 35(7): the applicable term for 35(6)(a): (a) conviction in England and Wales or Scotland 12 months; (b) in Northern Ireland 6 months.
-- src:2190 | (7) In subsection (6)(a) the applicable term is—
-- src:2191 | (a) for conviction in England and Wales or Scotland, 12 months;
-- src:2192 | (b) for conviction in Northern Ireland, 6 months.
@ref s 124 TCA 35(7) (src:2190-2192)
GIVEN `the place of conviction` IS A Place  @desc Where would you be convicted?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 124 TCA 35 term of imprisonment`
`s 124 TCA 35(7) the applicable term` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the place of conviction`
    WHEN `Greater London` THEN JUST `s 124 TCA 35(7)(a) a term of 12 months`
    WHEN `England outside Greater London` THEN JUST `s 124 TCA 35(7)(a) a term of 12 months`
    WHEN Wales THEN JUST `s 124 TCA 35(7)(a) a term of 12 months`
    WHEN Scotland THEN JUST `s 124 TCA 35(7)(a) a term of 12 months`
    WHEN `Northern Ireland` THEN JUST `s 124 TCA 35 a term of 6 months`
    WHEN `outside the United Kingdom` THEN NOTHING        -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (7) gives a term only for conviction in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland

-- 35(8): for an offence committed in England and Wales before section 281(5) of CJA2003 commenced, the 51 weeks in 35(4)(a) is read as 6 months.
-- src:2193 | (8) In relation to an offence under this section committed in England and Wales before the commencement of section 281(5) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003, the reference in subsection (4)(a) to 51 weeks is to be read as a reference to 6 months.
@ref s 124 TCA 35(8) (src:2193-2193)
GIVEN `the term` IS A `s 124 TCA 35 term of imprisonment`  @desc Which term applies to you?
      `the offence was committed in England and Wales before the commencement of section 281(5) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the offence committed in England and Wales before section 281(5) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003 came into force?
GIVETH A `s 124 TCA 35 term of imprisonment`
`s 124 TCA 35(8) the term as read for an offence committed before commencement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `s 124 TCA 35(4)(a) a term of 51 weeks` THEN
        IF `the offence was committed in England and Wales before the commencement of section 281(5) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003`
        THEN `s 124 TCA 35 a term of 6 months`
        ELSE `s 124 TCA 35(4)(a) a term of 51 weeks`
    WHEN `s 124 TCA 35 a term of 6 months` THEN `s 124 TCA 35 a term of 6 months`
    WHEN `s 124 TCA 35(7)(a) a term of 12 months` THEN `s 124 TCA 35(7)(a) a term of 12 months`
    WHEN `s 124 TCA 35(6)(b) a term of 7 years` THEN `s 124 TCA 35(6)(b) a term of 7 years`

-- 35(9): for an offence committed in England and Wales before section 154(1) of CJA2003 commenced, the 12 months in 35(7)(a) is read as 6 months.
-- src:2194 | (9) In relation to an offence under this section committed in England and Wales before the commencement of section 154(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003, the reference in subsection (7)(a) to 12 months is to be read as a reference to 6 months.
@ref s 124 TCA 35(9) (src:2194-2194)
GIVEN `the term` IS A `s 124 TCA 35 term of imprisonment`  @desc Which term applies to you?
      `the offence was committed in England and Wales before the commencement of section 154(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the offence committed in England and Wales before section 154(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003 came into force?
GIVETH A `s 124 TCA 35 term of imprisonment`
`s 124 TCA 35(9) the term as read for an offence committed before commencement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the term`
    WHEN `s 124 TCA 35(7)(a) a term of 12 months` THEN
        IF `the offence was committed in England and Wales before the commencement of section 154(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003`
        THEN `s 124 TCA 35 a term of 6 months`
        ELSE `s 124 TCA 35(7)(a) a term of 12 months`
    WHEN `s 124 TCA 35(4)(a) a term of 51 weeks` THEN `s 124 TCA 35(4)(a) a term of 51 weeks`
    WHEN `s 124 TCA 35 a term of 6 months` THEN `s 124 TCA 35 a term of 6 months`
    WHEN `s 124 TCA 35(6)(b) a term of 7 years` THEN `s 124 TCA 35(6)(b) a term of 7 years`

-- 35(3): on summary conviction pursuant to (2): imprisonment not exceeding the applicable term, or a fine not exceeding level 5, or both.
-- src:2182 | (3) A person who commits an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction pursuant to subsection (2) to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the applicable term, or a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale, or both.
@ref s 124 TCA 35(3) (src:2182-2182)
GIVEN `the place of conviction` IS A Place  @desc Where would you be convicted?
      `the offence was committed in England and Wales before the commencement of section 281(5) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the offence committed in England and Wales before section 281(5) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003 came into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 124 TCA 35 punishment`
`s 124 TCA 35(3) the greatest punishment on summary conviction for an offence triable summarily only` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 124 TCA 35(4) the applicable term` `the place of conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                             -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (4) gives a term only for conviction in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland
    WHEN JUST term THEN
        JUST (`s 124 TCA 35 punishment` WITH
            `the term of imprisonment not exceeded` IS `s 124 TCA 35(8) the term as read for an offence committed before commencement` term `the offence was committed in England and Wales before the commencement of section 281(5) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003`,
            `the fine not exceeded` IS `s 124 TCA 35(3) level 5 on the standard scale`)

-- 35(6)(a): on summary conviction pursuant to (5): imprisonment not exceeding the applicable term, or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum, or both.
-- src:2188 | (a) on summary conviction pursuant to subsection (5), to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the applicable term, or a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum, or both;
@ref s 124 TCA 35(6)(a) (src:2188-2188)
GIVEN `the place of conviction` IS A Place  @desc Where would you be convicted?
      `the offence was committed in England and Wales before the commencement of section 154(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Was the offence committed in England and Wales before section 154(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003 came into force?
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 124 TCA 35 punishment`
`s 124 TCA 35(6)(a) the greatest punishment on summary conviction for an offence triable either way` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 124 TCA 35(7) the applicable term` `the place of conviction`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                             -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (7) gives a term only for conviction in England and Wales, Scotland or Northern Ireland
    WHEN JUST term THEN
        JUST (`s 124 TCA 35 punishment` WITH
            `the term of imprisonment not exceeded` IS `s 124 TCA 35(9) the term as read for an offence committed before commencement` term `the offence was committed in England and Wales before the commencement of section 154(1) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003`,
            `the fine not exceeded` IS `s 124 TCA 35(6)(a) the statutory maximum`)

-- 35(6)(b): on conviction on indictment pursuant to (5): imprisonment not exceeding 7 years, or a fine, or both.
-- src:2189 | (b) on conviction on indictment pursuant to subsection (5) to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 7 years, or a fine, or both.
@ref s 124 TCA 35(6)(b) (src:2189-2189)
`s 124 TCA 35(6)(b) the greatest punishment on conviction on indictment` MEANS
    `s 124 TCA 35 punishment` WITH
        `the term of imprisonment not exceeded` IS `s 124 TCA 35(6)(b) a term of 7 years`,
        `the fine not exceeded` IS `s 124 TCA 35(6)(b) a fine without a stated limit`

§ `s 126 -- tax credits: transfer of functions (definitions)`

-- 126(11): "tax credits" are child tax credit or working tax credit or both. A closed definition.
-- src:2232 | (11) In this section references to tax credits are to child tax credit or working tax credit or both.
@ref s 126(11) (src:2232-2232)
GIVEN `the benefit` IS A Benefit  @desc Which benefit is in question?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 126(11) the benefit is a tax credit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the benefit`
    WHEN `child tax credit` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `working tax credit` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE                                       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "references to tax credits are to child tax credit or working tax credit or both"

-- 126(13): the defined terms.
-- src:2235 | “the Commissioners” means the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs;
@ref s 126(13) “the Commissioners” (src:2235-2235)
GIVEN `the body` IS AN Authority  @desc Which body is in question?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 126(13) the body is the Commissioners` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE                                       -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the Commissioners” means the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs"

DECLARE `s 126(13) kind of legislation` IS ONE OF
    `s 126(13) an Act, including the Welfare Reform Act 2012`
    `s 126(13) Northern Ireland legislation`
    `s 126(13) an instrument made under primary legislation, including an Order in Council under section 126`
    `s 126(13) some other kind of legislation`

-- src:2236 | “primary legislation” means an Act (including this Act) or Northern Ireland legislation;
@ref s 126(13) “primary legislation” (src:2236-2236)
GIVEN `the legislation` IS A `s 126(13) kind of legislation`  @desc What kind of legislation is it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 126(13) the legislation is primary legislation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the legislation`
    WHEN `s 126(13) an Act, including the Welfare Reform Act 2012` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 126(13) Northern Ireland legislation` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 126(13) an instrument made under primary legislation, including an Order in Council under section 126` THEN FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“primary legislation” means an Act (including this Act) or Northern Ireland legislation"
    WHEN `s 126(13) some other kind of legislation` THEN FALSE                                                                 -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“primary legislation” means an Act (including this Act) or Northern Ireland legislation"

-- src:2237 | “secondary legislation” means an instrument made under primary legislation (including an Order under this section);
@ref s 126(13) “secondary legislation” (src:2237-2237)
GIVEN `the legislation` IS A `s 126(13) kind of legislation`  @desc What kind of legislation is it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 126(13) the legislation is secondary legislation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the legislation`
    WHEN `s 126(13) an instrument made under primary legislation, including an Order in Council under section 126` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 126(13) an Act, including the Welfare Reform Act 2012` THEN FALSE            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“secondary legislation” means an instrument made under primary legislation (including an Order under this section)"
    WHEN `s 126(13) Northern Ireland legislation` THEN FALSE                              -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“secondary legislation” means an instrument made under primary legislation (including an Order under this section)"
    WHEN `s 126(13) some other kind of legislation` THEN FALSE                            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“secondary legislation” means an instrument made under primary legislation (including an Order under this section)"

-- src:2238 | “tax credit functions” means functions so far as relating to tax credits conferred by or under any primary or secondary legislation.
@ref s 126(13) “tax credit functions” (src:2238-2238)
GIVEN `the function relates to tax credits` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Does the function relate to child tax credit or working tax credit?
      `the function is conferred by or under primary or secondary legislation` IS A BOOLEAN  @desc Is the function conferred by or under an Act, Northern Ireland legislation or an instrument made under one?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 126(13) the function is a tax credit function` MEANS
    IF `the function relates to tax credits` AND `the function is conferred by or under primary or secondary legislation`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE FALSE                                            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“tax credit functions” means functions so far as relating to tax credits conferred by or under any primary or secondary legislation"
